{=============================================================================
  Roots compressor, 10 L (exercise)
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0202
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Teaching exercise, ULiège MSTh repetition R2, exercise 2 bis. A 10 L Roots
  compressor is tested at 1 bar and 20 °C suction, 1.4 bar discharge, with a
  volumetric efficiency of 85 % and a mechanical efficiency of 95 %. The
  equation window is that test point (inlet orifice, leakage nozzle, mixture).
  It does not contain the two sweeps asked in the statement. The file names
  no author.

  Inputs : V_s, P_su_0, T_su, P_ex, epsilon_v, eta_m, N, A_thr, gamma
  Outputs: M_dot, W_dot, W_dot_in, epsilon_s, A_thr_l
  Units  : SI - temperatures in °C, pressures in Pa, energies in J
  Source : ULiège MSTh, thermo_models, candidate TM-0036 - see README.md
  Status : failing - the inlet orifice cannot pass the fresh-charge flow
=============================================================================}

"!Statement"
"A Roots compressor of 10 litres displacement is tested as follows:"
"fluid: dry pure air; suction 1 bar and 20 °C; discharge 1.4 bar."
"The volumetric efficiency is 85 % and the mechanical efficiency is 95 %."
"Show how the volumetric and isentropic efficiencies could vary"
"with discharge pressure at constant speed, and with speed at constant"
"discharge pressure, and how the discharge temperature could vary in both cases."
"The equation window below is the test point only, as in the original."

"!Data"
V_s = 10E-3                                  "displacement [m^3]"
P_su_0 = 1E5                                 "suction pressure [Pa], 1 bar in the statement"
T_su = 20                                    "suction temperature [°C]"
P_ex = 1.4E5                                 "discharge pressure [Pa], 1.4 bar in the statement"
epsilon_v = 0.85                             "volumetric efficiency [-]"
eta_m = 0.95                                 "mechanical efficiency [-]"

"!Inlet orifice"
"Further hypothesis when the suction pressure drop is included, as in the original."
"The original also comments M_dot_l = 0.1577*M_dot and M_dot_l = 0.1*M_dot; those lines are not equations."
A_thr = 0.05^2/4*PI                          "inlet orifice area [m^2], diameter 5 cm as in the original"

"!Volume flow rates"
M_dot_in = M_dot + M_dot_l                   "mass balance [kg/s]"

"volumetric efficiency"
epsilon_v = V_dot_su/V_dot_s
V_dot_su = M_dot*v_su                        "actual fresh-charge volume flow [m^3/s]"
V_dot_s = M_dot_th*v_su                      "theoretical suction volume flow at the fresh-charge inlet state [m^3/s]"
V_dot_s = N*V_s
v_su = VOLUME(Air, T=T_su, P=P_su_0)         "specific volume of the fresh charge [m^3/kg]"

"hypothesis, as in the original"
N = 3000/60                                  "rotational speed [1/s]"

M_dot_in = V_dot_s/v_su_1                    "actual inlet volume flow after mixing [m^3/s]"
v_su_1 = VOLUME(Air, T=T_su_1, P=P_su_1)     "specific volume after mixing [m^3/kg]"
"The original comments the provisional closure v_su_1 = v_su. It is not an equation."

"!Power"
eta_m = W_dot_in/W_dot
W_dot_in = V_dot_s*(P_ex - P_su)             "Roots compressor characteristic [W]"

"!Overall isentropic efficiency"
epsilon_s = w_s/w                            "overall isentropic efficiency [-]"
w_s = h_ex_s - h_su_0                        "isentropic specific work [J/kg]"
h_ex_s = ENTHALPY(Air, s=s_su_0, P=P_ex)     "isentropic discharge enthalpy [J/kg]"
h_su_0 = ENTHALPY(Air, T=T_su)               "fresh-charge enthalpy [J/kg]"
s_su_0 = ENTROPY(Air, T=T_su, P=P_su_0)      "fresh-charge entropy [J/kg-K]"

W_dot = M_dot*w                              "shaft power from the fresh-charge flow [W]"

"!Suction pressure drop"
h_su_0 = h_thr + C_thr^2/2                   "steady-flow energy balance at the inlet throat [J/kg]"

h_thr = ENTHALPY(Air, s=s_su_0, P=P_thr)     "isentropic throat enthalpy [J/kg]"
P_thr = max(P_su, P_crit)                    "throat pressure, sonic cap as in the original [Pa]"
P_crit = (2/(gamma + 1))^(gamma/(gamma - 1))*p_su_0    "critical pressure [Pa]"
"The original comments the isentropic relation (T_thr+273)/(T_su+273) = (P_thr/P_su_0)^((gamma-1)/gamma)."
"provisional value, as in the original"
gamma = 1.4                                  "ratio of specific heats [-]"
T_thr = TEMPERATURE(Air, h=h_thr)            "throat temperature [°C]"

A_thr*C_thr = V_dot_thr
V_dot_thr = M_dot*v_thr                      "throat volume flow of the fresh charge [m^3/s]"
v_thr = VOLUME(Air, T=T_thr, P=P_thr)        "throat specific volume [m^3/kg]"

"The original comments the trials P_su = P_su_0 - 1E4 and P_su = P_su_0 (no suction pressure drop). They are not equations."
h_su = h_su_0                                "fresh-charge enthalpy used in the mixture [J/kg]"

"!Inlet state of the mixture"
"fictitious leakage nozzle, as in the original"
h_ex_1 = h_thr_l + C_thr_l^2/2               "energy balance in the leakage nozzle [J/kg]"

h_ex_1 = ENTHALPY(Air, s=s_su_1, P=P_ex)     "enthalpy at the leakage-nozzle inlet [J/kg]"
s_su_1 = ENTROPY(Air, h=h_su_1, P=P_su_1)    "entropy of the mixture [J/kg-K]"
"The original comments the provisional closure s_su_1 = s_su_0. It is not an equation."
T_su_1 = TEMPERATURE(Air, h=h_su_1)          "mixture temperature [°C]"
P_su_1 = P_su                                "pressure at the compressor inlet [Pa]"

M_dot*h_su + M_dot_l*h_ex_1 = M_dot_in*h_su_1    "mixture enthalpy at the compressor inlet [J/kg]"

h_thr_l = ENTHALPY(Air, s=s_ex_1, P=P_thr_l)     "isentropic expansion from the nozzle inlet to the throat [J/kg]"
s_ex_1 = ENTROPY(Air, h=h_ex_1, P=P_ex)          "entropy at the leakage-nozzle inlet [J/kg-K]"

"possible sonic regime, as in the original"
P_thr_l = max(P_crit_l, P_su)                "leakage-throat pressure [Pa]"
P_crit_l = (2/(gamma_l + 1))^(gamma_l/(gamma_l - 1))*p_ex    "critical leakage pressure [Pa]"
(T_thr_l + 273)/(T_ex_1 + 273) = (P_thr_l/P_ex)^((gamma_l - 1)/gamma_l)    "gamma from the isentropic relation, as in the original; +273 as written"
"The original comments the provisional value gamma_l = 1.4. It is not an equation."
T_ex_1 = TEMPERATURE(Air, h=h_ex_1)          "temperature at the leakage-nozzle inlet [°C]"
T_thr_l = TEMPERATURE(Air, h=h_thr_l)        "leakage-throat temperature [°C]"

"fictitious leakage opening, as in the original"
A_thr_l*C_thr_l = V_dot_thr_l
V_dot_thr_l = M_dot_l*v_thr_l                "leakage volume flow at the throat [m^3/s]"
v_thr_l = VOLUME(Air, T=T_thr_l, P=P_thr_l)  "leakage-throat specific volume [m^3/kg]"

"The original says the provisional approximations were left in so that parametric tables would run,"
"and that the 5 cm orifice gives a problem in the definition of h_thr."
"Commented trials (not equations) impose A_thr and A_thr_l, or set M_dot_l proportional to M_dot."
"Their recorded numbers are in the README. No parametric table is stored in the file."
